@*  ============================================================
    AUTHOR: PlantSafety Platform
    CREATED: 2026-07-14
    FILE DESCRIPTION: Project budget summary. Adapted from the original
      orphaned Components/ProjectPlanning/BudgetSummary.razor stub (distinct
      from the unrelated Components/Financials/BudgetSummary.razor owned by
      a different UI batch) and moved into Modules/PlanningProjects/Components
      (shared by the Planning Projects detail page and the Project Budgeting
      module). Built from the canonical Shared component library
      (CardComponent).
      GRACEFUL DEGRADATION: SafetyProjectDto only exposes a single
      PlannedBudget figure — there is no actual/committed spend or variance
      data available from the PlanningProjects backend (cost-actuals live in
      the separate Financials module, out of scope here). This component
      therefore renders Planned Budget only, plus a "needs backend wiring"
      note for the actual/variance figures, per the Blazor UI
      graceful-degradation rule.
      Pure/stateless/parameter-driven — no injected services.
    ============================================================ *@
<CardComponent Title="Budget Summary">
    <div class="ps-field-row">
        <span class="ps-field-label">Planned Budget</span>
        <span class="ps-field-value">@(PlannedBudget.HasValue ? PlannedBudget.Value.ToString("C", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture) : "Not set")</span>
    </div>
    <p class="ps-needs-backend">
        <span class="bi bi-exclamation-circle" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        Actual spend, committed spend, and variance need backend wiring — the PlanningProjects
        API currently exposes only the planned budget figure shown above.
    </p>
</CardComponent>

@code {
    /// <summary>The project's planned budget, or null when not set.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public decimal? PlannedBudget { get; set; }
}
